# fixedbugs, defect 2465 (panel 245's R2, provisional), 2026-11-11.
#
# SYMPTOM: `pick(1)` reads an `int64_t` past its `...` because its count says
# so, and a binding naming `pick` with its count alone handed it none: it
# built at exit 0 and printed `6126152376` at `-O0` and `6133359632` at `-O2`
# at batch 31's base (9febdd6c3), whatever the machine held there.
#
# FIX: a function its header declares variadic, bound with nothing past its
# `...`, is refused at the binding, `ffi_call_shape` (panel 245's R2, its D;
# `emit/ffi_bare_variadic.hero`): the route is a door of the program's own
# header, whose call is C's and whose arguments are the ones written there.
#
# The header is the program's own, so the case is judged on every platform.

extern "fixedbugs-2465-a-variadic-of-the-program-s-own-header-bound-bare.h"
    function pick(n: i64) -> i64  #~ ffi_call_shape

function main()
    print(pick(n: 1))
